The paper collage and pixel art finishes of the Motion Graphics engine (0.89: atelier.js, atelier-runtime.js) and
skills/drawing-craft.json restate the method of claude-drawing-skill (https://github.com/cloveric/claude-drawing-skill,
pinned 4886ed820dd11ba5e3f32fce0ad3560edba849db): SKILL.md (the process, the per-medium lists of failures and fixes, the
animation notes), lib/papercut.py (torn edges, the white fibrous rim, depth shadows, kraft, newsprint, notebook and crayon
papers) and lib/pixelart.py (a small grid, a limited palette, ordered Bayer dithering, a 3x5 bitmap font, nearest
upscaling). Its Python painting library is not included or run; the paper filters and pixel helpers are written for
the browser in our own code. The 4x4 Bayer matrix is the standard one. The MIT licence is kept in LICENSE beside this
notice.
